</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S3.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of the upwards traverse over BFS levels of the tree. Levels data is stored in arrays. The function <math id="S3.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> takes as input current value of carrying <math id="S3.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> (children), and current level data as parent <math id="S3.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and output new <math id="S3.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is passed up.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Myo: SSM layer as particular case</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that a normal SSM layer is a particular case of the proposed layer, hence Myo is more general.
Given a chain graph of length <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the following system <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T_{c}(\{(I,O,C_{v})\}_{v=1}^{L})x_{1:L}=u_{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{c}(\{(I,O,C_{v})\}_{v=1}^{L})x_{1:L}=u_{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S3.E13.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:155.3pt;height:81.4pt;vertical-align:-37.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(23.9pt,-12.5pt) scale(1.44552634495222,1.44552634495222) ;">
<p id="S3.E13.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.E13.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;O&amp;O&amp;&amp;\\
C_{2}&amp;I&amp;O&amp;&amp;\\
O&amp;C_{3}&amp;I&amp;\ddots&amp;\\
&amp;\ddots&amp;\ddots&amp;\ddots&amp;O\\
&amp;&amp;O&amp;C_{L}&amp;I\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}x_{\pi(1)}\\[3.99994pt]
\vdots\\[3.99994pt]
x_{\pi(L)}\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}u_{\pi(1)}\\[3.99994pt]
\vdots\\[3.99994pt]
u_{\pi(L)}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;O&amp;O&amp;&amp;\\
C_{2}&amp;I&amp;O&amp;&amp;\\
