<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix: Details of forward pass computation</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Myo: Shape Description</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we elaborate on the tensor shapes in the Myo layer. For concreteness, we consider a basic block: a parent that covers the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> child nodes, at some level <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> (the parent node is at level <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l+1</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}A^{l}_{1}&amp;O&amp;O&amp;B^{l}_{1}&amp;|&amp;u^{l}_{1}\\
\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;|&amp;\vdots\\
O&amp;O&amp;A^{l}_{k}&amp;B^{l}_{k}&amp;|&amp;u^{l}_{k}\\
C^{l}_{1}&amp;\dots&amp;C^{l}_{k}&amp;A^{l+1}_{[1;k]}&amp;|&amp;u^{l+1}_{[1;k]}\\
\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>O</mi></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}A^{l}_{1}&amp;O&amp;O&amp;B^{l}_{1}&amp;|&amp;u^{l}_{1}\\
\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;|&amp;\vdots\\
O&amp;O&amp;A^{l}_{k}&amp;B^{l}_{k}&amp;|&amp;u^{l}_{k}\\
C^{l}_{1}&amp;\dots&amp;C^{l}_{k}&amp;A^{l+1}_{[1;k]}&amp;|&amp;u^{l+1}_{[1;k]}\\
\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The choice of dimension of diagonal blocks fixes measurements of off-diagonal blocks. Given the input <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> with dimension <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{l}=r\times d_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{l}=r\times d_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, the size of the block can be equal to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{l},D_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{l},D_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> or apply a layer with block size <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d_{l},d_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d_{l},d_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> different vectors <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. On top of that, the layer can have a head dimension <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. application of different parameters to the same input.
Hence, the parameters of the layer <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by a length list <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (for each BFS layer), where each element <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> has dimensions <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,L_{l},d_{l},d_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,L_{l},d_{l},d_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> and input <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, with each element <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> with dimensions <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,L_{l},d_{l},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,L_{l},d_{l},r)</annotation></semantics></math> (one can add as many leading dimensions as desired, for example batch). Next we describe the algorithm in pseudo-code both abstract and python-style.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Pseudo-code</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide an abstract pseudocode without batch and head dimensions; see the next section <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Python style pseudo-code ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Details of forward pass computation ‣ Myosotis: structured computation for attention like layer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> for elaboration on them. We consider a tree <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> BFS layers, where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the level of the leaf and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> the level of the root. Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{1:L},\mathcal{B}_{1:L},\mathcal{C}_{1:L},\mathcal{U}_{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{1:L},\mathcal{B}_{1:L},\mathcal{C}_{1:L},\mathcal{U}_{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> be tuples of length <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{shape}(A_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>shape</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{shape}(A_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{l},d_{l},d_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{l},d_{l},d_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of nodes at the level <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the block. Then <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{shape}(B_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>shape</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{shape}(B_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{l},d_{l},d_{l+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{l},d_{l},d_{l+1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{shape}(B_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>shape</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{shape}(B_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{l},d_{l+1},d_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{l},d_{l+1},d_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{shape}(u_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>shape</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{shape}(u_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{l},d_{l},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{l},d_{l},r)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is a number of right parts, that is, we solve <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T[x^{1}_{1:L},\dots,x^{R}_{1:L}]=[u^{1}_{1:L},\dots,u^{R}_{1:L}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[x^{1}_{1:L},\dots,x^{R}_{1:L}]=[u^{1}_{1:L},\dots,u^{R}_{1:L}]</annotation></semantics></math>. We enumerate dimensions as <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,3)</annotation></semantics></math> and refer to them as numbers in pseudo-code where the function is applicable and as ":", where the function is vectorized.
We use <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">split</span> to denote splitting of the layer <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> array into chunks, where each chunk corresponds to the parent-child array at level <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l+1</annotation></semantics></math>. If a tree is complete, then the BFS ordering guarantees that this holds; otherwise, it is always possible to sort branches not from the first level at most right of the tree.


<span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage" style="width:165.6pt;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_align_top">
              
<span id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<span class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Upward Traverse</span>
<span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<span id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">1</span></span>
                      
                      
                    <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">procedure</span><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:70%;">UpF</span><span id="alg1.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(</span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{k},B_{k},C_{k},u_{k}\}_{k\in\{c,p\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">C</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">u</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{k},B_{k},C_{k},u_{k}\}_{k\in\{c,p\}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">)
</span>
</span>
<span id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">2</span></span>
                      
                      
                    <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">   </span><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{B}_{c}\leftarrow-\text{Solve}_{:,2,3}(A_{c},B_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><msub><mtext mathsize="0.700em">Solve</mtext><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">3</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{B}_{c}\leftarrow-\text{Solve}_{:,2,3}(A_{c},B_{c})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">
</span>
</span>
<span id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">3</span></span>
                      
                      
