<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Datasets description</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MNIST</span>: 10-way (0-9 digits) classification of a <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="28\times 28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">28\times 28</annotation></semantics></math> grayscale image of a handwritten digit. The input image is flattened into a <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="784" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>784</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">784</annotation></semantics></math>-length scalar sequence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CIFAR</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>: 10-way image classification using the CIFAR-10 dataset The input is flattened into a sequence of inputs of <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math>-length and three-channel triple (R,G,B). There are <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45,000</annotation></semantics></math> training examples, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5,000</annotation></semantics></math> validation examples, and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10,000</annotation></semantics></math> test examples.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both datasets are flattened in common sequential versions: sMNIST, sCIFAR with snake order, and in quad-tree aligned versions: zMNIST, zCIFAR wth morton order, see Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.4 Datasets description ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Details of forward pass computation ‣ Myosotis: structured computation for attention like layer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></p>
</div>
